# Soros Fund Management

Office address: 250 W 55th St, New York, NY 10019  
Website: sorosfundmgmt.com  
Year established: 1970  
Company type: financial services  
Employees: 200+  
Expertise: public equity, private equity, credit (investment-grade to distressed), fixed income, foreign exchange, alternative assets, macro trading, external manager allocation, direct lending, real estate financing  
Parent company: N/A  
Key people: Dawn Fitzpatrick (CEO), Mahendar Rajani (COO), Brenda Formes (chief administrative officer), Andy Hollenbeck (general counsel), Alex Potter (CTO), Matthew Wain (chief risk officer), Phil DeSantis (global head of credit)  
Financing status: privately held family office [...] Soros Fund Management LLC is a New York City-based family office and global asset manager. The company oversees $28 billion in assets and serves as the main asset manager for the Open Society Foundations, a global charitable organization. SFM also has offices in Greenwich, Garden City, London, and Dublin, with 200 employees worldwide.

## History of Soros Fund Management

Soros Fund Management was founded by George Soros, a Hungarian-born investor who came to the US in 1956. He started his hedge fund in 1970, and it grew into one of America's most successful investment firms.

### The Quantum Fund era

The company gained recognition in 1973 when Soros partnered with Jim Rogers to co-found the Quantum Fund. The fund took a different approach to investing at the time.",Soros Fund Management | Home,,,2026-07-28T09:52:18.646023,Soros Fund Management,,Validation score: 4,Needs Review,,,EXISTING,,,,"SFM invests with agility and conviction across a wide range of strategies and asset classes, managing capital with a long-term, high-return focus.",Tavily,,[],"Soros Fund Management | Home Disciplined Capital Strategic Investing Quality Returns Soros Fund Management is a global asset manager and family office that serves as the principal asset manager for the Open Society Foundations. With a permanent capital base and 50+ years of experience, we invest across all asset classes and a broad set of strategies — driven by opportunity, smart risk-taking, and a commitment to generating high-quality returns. Investment Expertise on a Global Scale Our resources, reach, and experienced team provide the insight needed for stable, long-term growth. $28B Assets Under Management (AUM) 50+ Years of Experience 200 Employees 5 Offices “With over three decades in the finance industry, I deeply appreciate just how unique Soros Fund Management is and what a privilege it is to work here. The advantages afforded to us have allowed us to attract and build upon a durable team of top tier talent — whom I genuinely enjoy sitting shoulder to shoulder with — and a mindset that there is always more for us to capitalize on.” Dawn Fitzpatrick, Chief Executive Officer and Chief Investment Officer Meet Our Leadership What We Do Investing with Patience. Acting with Conviction. Our agile and long-term approach allows us to invest globally in a wide range of strategies and asset classes, including public and private equity and credit, fixed income, foreign exchange, and alternative assets. As a strategic asset allocator and trusted liquidity provider, we manage capital internally while also partnering with top-tier external investors to seize opportunities and drive long-term value. More on What We Do Careers One Team, Collaborating for Impact We believe investing in our people drives better outcomes in markets. Transparency, open debate, and direct engagement with senior leadership at all levels of the organization are core to how we operate. We foster a culture where ideas drive impact, empowering employees to work across teams, collaborate, and continuously grow. Explore Careers About History of Success, True to Our Values Founded by George Soros over 50 years ago, Soros Fund Management has a long history of success and today is a leading global asset manager. By leveraging deep industry expertise, we build conviction and act decisively, often taking large, concentrated positions when opportunities arise. With an unconstrained mandate, we allocate capital dynamically to opportunities, all while upholding our core values. More About Us Mission Impact Fueling Solutions to Today’s Most Pressing Issues We seek to be part of the solution, not just to avoid being part of the problem. Our impact is measured by both the returns we generate and the values we uphold, from environmental stewardship to social responsibility. Today, our work is helping drive the clean energy transition, combat economic inequalities, ensure freedom of expression, and promote democratic practices and rights. Explore Our Mission Impact Core Values Our principles form the foundation of everything that we do, guiding our commitment to integrity, teamwork, and purpose-driven investing. At Soros Fund Management, collaboration and diversity of thought are not just ideals; they give us a competitive edge, enabling us to navigate complexity, uncover opportunities, and drive impact. Smart Risk-Taking We make bold yet calculated decisions that drive capital growth and innovation, evaluating risks with rigor and clarity to balance opportunity with responsibility. While not every outcome will go our way, we remain committed to this process. This approach empowers us to pursue new avenues while maintaining a strong foundation. Owner’s Mindset We approach decisions with a sense of accountability, purpose, and commitment. By taking a long-term view, we emphasize responsibility and stewardship to ensure sustainable growth and positive impact. Teamwork Collaboration is at the core of our success, with each team member bringing unique strengths and perspectives that enhance our overall impact. By working together, we create solutions that are greater than the sum of their parts. Humility We recognize that success is a collective effort, and we value every perspective, always staying open to new insights. By embracing humility, we remain grounded, adaptable, and focused on listening — learning from both success and failure and continuously improving. Integrity We hold ourselves to the highest ethical standards, prioritizing honesty, transparency, and accountability. Our commitment and consistency in doing what is right builds trust and reinforces our guiding principles. Important Notice : Fraudulent Schemes Impersonating Soros Fund Management (“SFM”) More Info Soros Fund Management (“SFM”) has recently become aware of fraudulent activity involving individuals and groups falsely claiming to be affiliated with SFM on social media platforms, email and messaging applications, and fraudulent websites. The deceptive conduct includes impersonating SFM employees, soliciting individuals to participate in investment activities, and using fake domains, email accounts, or online profiles that appear connected to SFM. These activities are entirely unauthorized and are not affiliated with SFM in any way. SFM is a family office and does not seek, solicit or accept investors that are not eligible family clients. SFM does not solicit investment opportunities through social media platforms, messaging applications, or similar channels. Legitimate business communications from SFM will come only from official @soros.com email addresses. Emails from any other domains claiming to represent SFM are not authorized and should be treated as fraudulent and disregarded. SFM and its partners, employees, directors, officers, advisors, successors, and agents are not responsible for the conduct, services, or information provided by unauthorized third parties. If you believe you or someone you know has been targeted or affected by fraudulent activity, please report it to your local law enforcement authorities or relevant regulatory agencies. Leadership: Built on Trust and Transparency Expertise Innovation Impact Our leadership team combines deep expertise with a culture that values intellectual rigor, transparency, and accountability. By fostering an environment where smart people challenge and support one another, our leaders drive investment excellence while capitalizing on the unique aspects of Soros Fund Management — including a flexible, patient approach to investing. This accessibility and commitment to the team and our clients ensure we remain ahead of the curve in global investment strategies. Dawn Fitzpatrick Chief Executive Officer and Chief Investment Officer Mahendar Rajani Chief Operating Officer Neil Pegrum Global Head of Equities and Head of London Office Phil DeSantis Global Head of Credit Lucy DeStefano Global Head of Trade Execution and Co-Head of Macro Investing Brenda Formes Chief Administrative Officer Andy Hollenbeck General Counsel and Chief Compliance Officer Hilary Irby Chief Sustainability Officer and Head of Impact Strategy Matt Mallgrave Global Head of Equity Capital Markets Alex Potter Chief Technology Officer Matthew Wain Chief Risk Officer Important Notice : Fraudulent Schemes Impersonating Soros Fund Management (“SFM”) More Info Soros Fund Management (“SFM”) has recently become aware of fraudulent activity involving individuals and groups falsely claiming to be affiliated with SFM on social media platforms, email and messaging applications, and fraudulent websites. The deceptive conduct includes impersonating SFM employees, soliciting individuals to participate in investment activities, and using fake domains, email accounts, or online profiles that appear connected to SFM. These activities are entirely unauthorized and are not affiliated with SFM in any way. SFM is a family office and does not seek, solicit or accept investors that are not eligible family clients. SFM does not solicit in",
