Managing Director, IR & Strategic Communications",Praxis Rock · Capital Intelligence for Private Markets,,,2026-07-28T09:52:45.725280,Praxis Rock ADVISORS,,Validation score: 1,Rejected,,,EXISTING,,,,"A relationship graph of 2.5M+ people, built from primary sources, powers fundraising and deal origination across 55+ verticals. All data transfers to clients.",Tavily,,[],"Praxis Rock · Capital Intelligence for Private Markets Skip to main content Schedule a Conversation Capital Intelligence for Private Markets Schedule a Conversation Praxis Rock Advisors is a capital intelligence platform for private markets, built to replace manual fundraising and deal sourcing with autonomous infrastructure. Most capital formation and deal sourcing still runs on the same manual process: buy a target list, lean on your network, make phone calls, and send emails that land cold more often than not. We built the platform that replaces it. Finds the right institution, the right person inside it, the real path connecting you to them. Writes the message the way you'd write it yourself, and sends it under your name. Built by practitioners from The Carlyle Group, Deutsche Bank, JPMorgan, and Bank of America. 100+ Clients 2.5M+ People Mapped 55+ Sectors Covered $1.5B+ Capital Facilitated THE PLATFORM Two Programs. One Intelligence Platform. Praxis Rock Advisors is a capital intelligence platform for private markets, built on decades of operating experience across institutional fundraising and deal origination. Capital intelligence is the deployment of autonomous AI systems to identify, qualify, and engage the specific individuals who determine whether a transaction moves forward. It operates on primary data that commercial databases have not indexed, spanning both institutional allocators and acquisition targets. This is not analytics layered on top of existing data. It is a new class of sourcing infrastructure. The problem is well known to anyone who has run a fundraise or built an acquisition pipeline. Teams spend months compiling target lists from the same commercial platforms, manually researching contact paths, and coordinating outreach across disconnected tools. The process absorbs significant time and headcount before a single qualified conversation takes place. We built a system that consolidates the entire workflow. The platform identifies the right individual at the right institution, maps the relationship path connecting you to that person, and executes a full outreach program under your brand. Not a lead list. Not a CRM integration. A complete program, from initial sourcing through a confirmed first meeting. Firms that prefer to run the system themselves can now operate the platform directly. The platform operates through two modules. Capital formation serves fund managers and corporates raising institutional capital, including PE fundraising . Deal origination serves acquirers sourcing proprietary targets. Both run on the same core infrastructure: autonomous agents that work primary data sources outside the coverage of established databases. And this is the central design choice. The commercial databases that most firms rely on recycle the same records across the same subscriber base. The data degrades over time, and the coverage gaps are structural, not incidental. We built a proprietary data layer because the existing options did not meet the standard required for programmatic outreach at this level. Read more Capital Formation Capital Intelligence for Institutional Fundraising Finding the right institution is the easy part. The fundraising module goes to the decision-maker inside it, built from primary regulatory filings and hundreds of proprietary data pipelines. Then it handles everything that follows. Function. Mandate authority. Check size range. Trust path from your team to that person. Outreach drafted around the specific connection. Executed under your brand, in your voice. Praxis Rock's institutional fundraising programs → Deal Origination Proprietary Acquisition Target Intelligence Every firm working from the same commercial database is working from the same list. The origination engine builds from primary sources those databases miss. Each target classified by what the business actually does today, not a registration-era code. Profiled against what matters to you. Path to the owner. Outreach drafted in your voice around the deal thesis and the connection that makes it credible. Executed under your brand, as a principal. Proprietary deal origination for PE firms and acquirers → Programs Executed For Private Equity Firms Independent Sponsors Holding Companies Family Offices Hedge Funds Venture Capital Firms Real Estate Firms Corporate Acquirers Startups Growth-Stage Companies WHY PRAXIS ROCK The Platform's Origin Praxis Rock wasn't built by a product team. Jeff came out of Deutsche Bank, The World Bank, ARIS Capital, and The Carlyle Group with 25+ years of capital markets expertise . Steve ran capital markets groups at JPMorgan, Bank of America, and Royal Bank of Scotland. Together, with their partner Dave, they built RueOne, an independent PE firm . Hundreds of transactions and fundraising mandates , for their own funds and for others. Both sides of every table. They ran through every technology that existed for this problem. Commercial databases, custom data pipelines, AI enrichment, delivery infrastructure. Years of it. What worked, what didn't. Commercial databases are built for everywhere, which means they work perfectly for nowhere. So they built their own. And they kept hitting the same wall. The right institution, the wrong contact. The right contact, no credible path in. The right path, no system to execute it at scale. They built the autonomous agent infrastructure and trust graph for themselves. It became Praxis Rock. One platform. Two programs. Ready to run for you. Schedule a Conversation Top 100 Private Equity Firms by AUM (2026 Rankings) | Praxis Rock Skip to main content Schedule a Conversation Deal Origination Top 100 Private Equity Firms: 2026 Rankings by AUM Jeff Baehr · Mar 2026 · 45 min read Last updated July 12, 2026 The five largest alternative asset managers with major PE platforms are Blackstone ($1.3 trillion), Apollo ($938 billion), KKR ($744 billion), Ares ($623 billion), and Brookfield ($603 billion fee-bearing). The top five control over $4 trillion. The global PE industry manages roughly $8 trillion, with $2 trillion in dry powder. Fundraising has concentrated sharply: the 10 largest fund closes in 2025 captured 46% of all capital raised, while total fund count fell 18%. This ranking covers 100 firms across every tier, with verified AUM data from Q4 2025 earnings reports, SEC filings, and press releases. Executive Summary Private equity manages roughly $8 trillion globally. Five years ago, that number was $4 trillion. The firms at the top of this ranking are responsible for most of that growth, and they look nothing like the buyout shops they were a decade ago. Blackstone manages $1.3 trillion. Apollo is approaching $1 trillion. KKR crossed $744 billion. These are alternative asset platforms where traditional buyouts represent one strategy among credit, infrastructure, real estate, and insurance solutions. Blackstone's private equity business accounts for roughly $350 billion of its $1.3 trillion total. The rest is credit, real estate, infrastructure, and hedge fund solutions. When someone says ""Blackstone is a PE firm,"" they're describing about 27% of the business. This matters because the firms you're competing against, partnering with, or pitching to aren't operating in the world most people imagine when they hear ""private equity."" The capital structures are different. The deployment timelines are different. The return expectations are different. This ranking covers 100 firms by total assets under management, from trillion-dollar platforms to middle-market operators managing focused strategies. AUM figures are verified through Q4 2025 earnings reports, SEC filings, and press releases where available. Estimates are noted. The Full Rankings: Top 100 PE Firms by AUM AUM figures are as of December 31, 2025 unless noted. Estimates are marked with (~). Brookfield's figure represents fee-bearing capital at the BAM level; corporate AUM exceeds $1 trillion. Rank Firm AUM HQ Founded Primary St",
