 Who are the Reimann family?",JAB Holding Company — Family Office Profile | PipelineRoad,,,2026-07-28T09:52:45.725280,Reimann Family Office (JAB Holding),,Validation score: 4,Needs Review,,,EXISTING,,,,"JAB Holding Company is the investment vehicle of the Reimann family of Germany, managing approximately $25 billion in assets with major holdings in…",Tavily,,[],"JAB Holding Company — Family Office Profile | PipelineRoad Platform Pricing Solutions Fund Managers LPs & Family Offices Startups Search Funds Use Cases Investor Outreach Capital Raising Fund Marketing LP Database Resources Insights & Research News New Glossary Calculators & Tools LP Directory Event Directory Compare vs Affinity vs Dynamo vs DealCloud Join Waitlist Assets Under Management $25B As of 2024-12-31 Alternatives Allocation 65% of total portfolio Headquarters Luxembourg, Luxembourg Asset Classes Private Equity Public Equities Consumer Brands Real Estate www.jabholco.com ↗ JAB Holding Company is the principal investment vehicle of the Reimann family of Germany, managing approximately $25 billion in assets from its headquarters in Luxembourg. The firm has built one of the most significant consumer brand portfolios in the world, with major holdings spanning coffee, restaurants, beauty, and pet care. JAB is managed by a professional investment team led by Olivier Goudet, operating independently of the family’s day-to-day involvement. Investment Strategy JAB Holding’s investment strategy centers on acquiring and building leading consumer-facing businesses with strong brands, recurring revenue characteristics, and global scale potential. The firm’s approach is distinct from traditional private equity : JAB takes long-term, controlling positions in businesses and manages them as a permanent owner rather than seeking exits within a defined fund lifecycle . The firm’s most visible investment theme has been coffee. Over the past fifteen years, JAB systematically assembled a global coffee empire through the acquisitions of Peet’s Coffee, Jacobs Douwe Egberts (now JDE Peet’s), Keurig Green Mountain (merged with Dr Pepper Snapple to form Keurig Dr Pepper), Caribou Coffee, and Stumptown Coffee Roasters. This consolidation strategy created one of the largest coffee companies in the world and demonstrated JAB’s ability to execute complex, multi-billion-dollar transactions across geographies. Beyond coffee, JAB has built positions in quick-service restaurants (Panera Brands, Pret A Manger, Krispy Kreme), beauty and fragrance (Coty), and pet care (National Veterinary Associates). These investments share common characteristics: strong consumer brands, subscription or repeat-purchase dynamics, and opportunities for operational improvement and geographic expansion. The Reimann family’s wealth originated from their stake in Benckiser, the German chemicals company that merged with Reckitt & Colman to form Reckitt Benckiser (now Reckitt). The family gradually sold down their Reckitt position and redeployed capital into consumer brands through JAB, executing one of the most successful wealth diversification strategies in European family office history. Private Markets Approach JAB Holding is one of the most active family-backed private equity investors globally. The firm operates through multiple investment vehicles, including JAB Consumer Partners (which raises capital from external investors alongside family capital) and direct balance sheet investments. This hybrid structure allows JAB to deploy significantly more capital than the family’s wealth alone would permit. JAB Consumer Partners has raised multiple funds focused on consumer investments, attracting institutional LPs alongside the Reimann family’s capital. This fundraising capability gives JAB the firepower to compete for large-scale transactions against the biggest private equity firms. The firm’s deal execution is characterized by large transaction sizes, leverage, and active post-acquisition management. JAB installs professional management teams, drives cost synergies across its portfolio, and invests in digital transformation and brand building. The integration of Keurig and Dr Pepper Snapple into Keurig Dr Pepper is a prime example of JAB’s ability to create value through strategic combinations. JAB has also navigated portfolio challenges, including the restructuring of its Coty investment and the partial divestiture of some restaurant brands. These adjustments reflect the inherent difficulty of managing a large, leveraged consumer portfolio through economic cycles and shifting consumer preferences. The firm’s Luxembourg domicile provides tax efficiency and governance flexibility, while the professional management structure allows the Reimann family to maintain a low public profile. The family has been deliberate in separating its personal activities from JAB’s corporate operations, allowing the investment team to operate with institutional discipline. FAQ Frequently Asked Questions What is JAB Holding Company? JAB Holding Company is a privately held investment company based in Luxembourg that manages the wealth of the Reimann family of Germany. The firm is best known for assembling one of the world's largest coffee empires, with holdings including Keurig Dr Pepper, JDE Peet's (Jacobs Douwe Egberts), Peet's Coffee, and Krispy Kreme. JAB also holds significant positions in luxury goods and pet care. Who are the Reimann family? The Reimann family are the descendants of Ludwig Reimann, co-founder of the German chemicals company Benckiser. The family's wealth originated from Reckitt Benckiser (now Reckitt) and was diversified into consumer brands through JAB Holding. The family maintains a low public profile and manages their investments through JAB's professional management team led by Olivier Goudet. What companies does JAB Holding own? JAB's major holdings include Keurig Dr Pepper (publicly traded, significant stake), JDE Peet's (global coffee company), Krispy Kreme, Panera Brands, Pret A Manger, Coty (beauty and fragrance), and NVA (National Veterinary Associates). The portfolio spans coffee, restaurants, beauty, and pet care. Related Resources Tool Fund Performance Benchmark Compare returns across PE, VC, and real estate strategies. Tool IRR Calculator Calculate internal rate of return for fund investments. Guide How to Raise a Private Equity Fund Step-by-step guide covering LP targeting, due diligence, and first close. Guide LP Discovery Playbook Strategies for identifying and engaging institutional allocators. Directory Browse All LP Profiles 1,600+ institutional investor profiles with allocation data. Similar Family Offices M Mousse Partners S Soros Fund Management L Lauder Family Office W Willett Advisors G GenSpring Family Offices S Safra Group Raising a fund? PipelineRoad matches GPs with active allocators. Join Waitlist PIPELINEROAD AI-powered capital raising for emerging fund managers. Thesis-driven investor matching across 30+ institutional data sources. Ask AI about us Capital raising intelligence. LP trends, allocation data, and fundraising strategies. No spam. Subscribe You're in. Watch your inbox for weekly LP intelligence. Platform Investor Database Smart Outreach Investor Matching How It Works Pricing Solutions Fund Managers LPs & Family Offices Startups Search Funds Investor Outreach Capital Raising Fund Marketing Capital Introduction LP Database Emerging Managers PE CRM VC CRM PE Software AI for PE Resources News Blog Glossary Calculators & Tools LP Directory Fund Manager Directory LP Rankings & Lists Research & Reports Event Directory Fundraising Guide Placement Agent Guide DDQ Template Fund Terms Generator Investor Updates Compare All Comparisons vs Affinity vs Dynamo vs DealCloud vs Altvia vs Juniper Square vs 4Degrees vs Dakota PitchBook Alternatives CRM Comparison Company About Contact RSS Feed Glossary Carried Interest Capital Call Management Fee Preferred Return J-Curve Waterfall Dry Powder Placement Agent © 2026 Pi