# Company Profile

## MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office)

##### Company Overview [...] Our mission is to enhance the long-term wealth of our investors, and one of our core values is to put the interests of our investors ahead of our own. As a result, we only create and/or offer products and services to our investors that we truly believe adds material value to their long-term wealth. Unlike other asset managers, we have no mandate to build assets under management or enterprise value. In addition, we only manage assets for and advise McKinsey related clients; we do not accept outside or third-party investments.   
  
MIO is a 120-person organization, with team members principally located in New York, and with small presences in London, Munich, and Singapore. We are a wholly owned subsidiary of McKinsey, but our activities are kept entirely separate to those of the Firm.","MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) Employer Profile - Professional Risk Managers' International Association",,,2026-07-28T09:53:54.302205,McKinsey Investment Office,,Validation score: 6,Verified,,,EXISTING,,,,"Is MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) hiring? Learn more about available jobs and working at MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) on Professional Risk Managers' International Association.",Tavily,,[],"MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) Employer Profile - Professional Risk Managers' International Association Career Center Home Company Directory Company Profile Company Profile MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) Company Overview MIO Partners, Inc. (“MIO”), the investment management subsidiary or “family office” of McKinsey & Company, Inc. (“McKinsey” or “the Firm”) manages a multi-billion dollar portfolio of assets for the Firm, its partners, former partners, and employees. Assets are invested in a broad range of traditional and alternative asset strategies, principally with third-party managers. MIO implements investments in three main forms: fund-of-funds investing, separately managed accounts, and direct trades (which are mostly macro-oriented, derivatives-based trades). We also have a Client Service & Advisory team that helps the Firm’s partners with accessing our investment products and constructing overall portfolios to suit their individual needs. Our mission is to enhance the long-term wealth of our investors, and one of our core values is to put the interests of our investors ahead of our own. As a result, we only create and/or offer products and services to our investors that we truly believe adds material value to their long-term wealth. Unlike other asset managers, we have no mandate to build assets under management or enterprise value. In addition, we only manage assets for and advise McKinsey related clients; we do not accept outside or third-party investments. MIO is a 120-person organization, with team members principally located in New York, and with small presences in London, Munich, and Singapore. We are a wholly owned subsidiary of McKinsey, but our activities are kept entirely separate to those of the Firm. Company History MIO Partners, Inc. (McKinsey Investment Office) is the wholly-owned legal subsidiary of McKinsey & Company (the global management consulting firm). Basic Information Parent: McKinsey & Company Employees: 120 Industry: Finance Location: New York, New York, United States Positions Available Sort by: Position ▲ Date Location Show All Details This company currently has no jobs posted. Click here to search for jobs. Insert additional messaging here.",
