for certain clients’ trading teams Hedging & financing: Liquidity and hedging for illiquid or concentrated assets Acquisition & disposal: Strategies for large, concentrated or illiquid public and private assets Portfolio analytics : Institutional-level analytics, actionable strategies and best practices for family offices. The Family Office Group also offers advisory services based on our direct experience of setting up, structuring and running institutional-sized private investment companies and family offices. Best Global Private Bank for Family Offices* Citi Private Bank was awarded Best Global Private Bank for Family Offices by PWM and The Banker at their 2025 Global Private Banking Awards. * Comprehensive services for your wealth All management Investment legacy lifestyle Insights Read some of our insights into the key issues for you and your wealth. View all insights FAMILY OFFICE AI in the Family Office: Navigating Privacy, Efficiency and Institutional Rigor CITI INSTITUTE - FAMILY OFFICE GROUP May 12, 2026 The age of the intelligent, automated family office has arrived. The question is no longer whether to adopt AI, but how to navigate the journey thoughtfully and effectively. Learn more about AI in the Family Office: Navigating Privacy, Efficiency and Institutional Rigor FAMILY OFFICE Best Practices to Sustain Family Wealth Across Generations FAMILY OFFICE GROUP March 27, 2026 As a phenomenon, the dissipation or loss of family wealth is almost as old as wealth itself and prevalent throughout the world. Indeed, almost every culture has a longstanding saying equivalent to the adage of “shirtsleeves to shirtsleeves in three generations.” In recent decades, research has shown the tendency of great wealth to fail to survive beyond the third generation. According to one study, 90% of wealth transfers fail by the third generation. Learn more about Best Practices to Sustain Family Wealth Across Generations FAMILY OFFICE Enhancing Personal Safety and Security FAMILY OFFICE GROUP March 27, 2026 The importance of maintaining personal privacy and security has grown exponentially for wealthy individuals and their families in an era of accelerating technological change and continuously emerging and expanding threats. A robust security strategy and understanding of the evolving threat landscape is essential to proactively protect themselves, their families and their assets. Learn more about Enhancing Personal Safety and Security FAMILY OFFICE 2025 Global Family Office Report FAMILY OFFICE GROUP September 16, 2025 Our seventh annual Global Family Office Report provides fresh insights into how our sophisticated clients are preserving and growing generational wealth in today’s often unsettled world. Learn more about 2025 Global Family Office Report Insights Read some of our insights into the key issues for you and your wealth. View all insights Meet our people Global Head Alexandre Monnier Family Office Advisory Head View bio of Alexandre Monnier Meet our wealth expert Alexandre has responsibility for serving for family office clients, guiding them with advice, education, events and networking opportunities. Previously, Alexandre was Head of Wealth Sustainability and President of the Institute for Family Success at Hawthorn, the Multi-Family Office of PNC, providing integrated wealth management services to ultra-high net worth family offices. Prior to that, he was President of Family Office Exchange (FOX), a private network for wealth owning families. In that role, he helped family offices in different countries with the unique challenges inherent to wealth ownership, including family vision, governance, next-generation education, leadership succession, risk management, wealth management and family office practices. Alexandre is a graduate of ESCP Europe/European School of Management. He has also been a member of Young Presidents’ Organization (YPO) since 2005. Global Head Karen Kardos Philanthropic Advisory Head Karen's LinkedIn profile View bio of Karen Kardos Meet our wealth expert Karen provides philanthropic advice and services to families, foundations, and endowments on strategic development and best practices to meet their philanthropic goals. Previously, Karen served for 10 years as the Director of Finance and Philanthropic Operations for a private foundation in the multifamily office practice of Geller & Co. In addition to advising clients on philanthropic strategies, she is also well versed in private foundation operations, governance, and compliance. Karen is a 21/64 Multigenerational Advisor. She holds a bachelor’s degree in accounting from Binghamton University. Global Head Betsy Bickar Art Advisory Head View bio of Betsy Bickar Meet our wealth expert Betsy leads a team of art advisors that helps clients build and manage museum-quality art collections. With experience gained in some of the world’s most prestigious galleries, auction houses and museums, her team’s expertise covers many international collecting fields. Betsy specializes in post-war, contemporary and emerging art, with additional strengths in Latin American, American and modern art. She started her career at a private Latin American art collection and foundation. Subsequently, she held roles at the Pace Gallery and Sean Kelly Gallery, among others, and founded an internationally recognized exhibition space in San José, Costa Rica. She regularly contributes insights to art publications and major media outlets. Betsy graduated with a double major in art history and German language from The Ohio State University. The World's Changemakers The world's changemakers community exists to help make the world a better place. It is our privilege to share this selection of stories about their accomplishments. Elton John & David Furnish By replacing stigmatization with care and compassion, the Elton John AIDS Foundation aims to help put an end to the AIDS epidemic by 2030. Learn more Elton John & David Furnish Global Citizens Kindness is the greatest healer Elton John & David Furnish For the past 30 years, the Elton John AIDS Foundation has worked tirelessly to put an end to the disease that has now claimed at least 38 million lives over some decades. (The true figure is likely higher owing to persistent under-recording.) Inspired partly by the bravery of Ryan White, a young boy who died of AIDS after a contaminated blood transfusion, Elton decided to commit himself to the struggle against this cruel blight on humanity. Learn more Elton John & David Furnish Mabel va",
