##### Operations and Administration",Family Office Recruitment - Eagle Private,,,2026-07-28T09:54:19.812774,For Hiring an M&A Advisor,,Validation score: 6,Verified,,,EXISTING,,,,"Eagle Private are specialist family office recruiters, placing investment, finance, legal and operational professionals within single and multi-family offices globally. Trusted. Discreet. Expert.",Tavily,,[],"Family Office Recruitment - Eagle Private Family Office Recruitment Finding the right person for a family office is a distinctive challenge. The dynamics are different, the expectations are higher, and the consequences of getting it wrong run deeper – both professionally and personally. Eagle Private operate as family office recruiters, working exclusively within the private wealth and family office space, with an extensive network of family office professionals around the world. What Family Office Recruitment Involves Family office recruitment is the process of identifying, assessing and placing executives, investment professionals, finance leaders, legal advisors and operational staff within single family offices, multi-family offices, and private offices serving ultra-high-net-worth principals. This type of recruitment is highly unique in its approach, as each family office setting is often entirely distinct. Family offices have a high level of discretion, and each hiring decision is personal – a Chief Investment Officer or Chief of Staff in a family office will work closely with the Principal, their family and in many cases their most trusted advisors. The cultural alignment of each individual and interpersonal fit are as important as qualifications. Our family office recruitment firm goes beyond the traditional executive search methodology. We have a deep understanding of how family office structures work, what Principals actually require (other than what’s written in the brief), and a global network of professionals built through years of experience working in the industry. As a family office recruitment agency, we act as a trusted and confidential intermediary, between Principals and an exceptionally curated talent pool, making introductions we genuinely believe will strengthen those around you, and the legacy you’re building across generations. The Process: From Brief to Placement Every assignment we take on follows a rigorous, personal and highly discrete process, underpinned by relationships built on trust and a genuine understanding of the family office space. At Eagle Private, this is how we operate as family office recruiters. Initial Consultation / Needs Analysis We meet with the client (in person where possible) to develop and understand the organisation, its structure, culture, the Principal’s working style, and what success looks like in the first six to twelve months. Position Profile We help clients articulate exactly what they’re looking for, providing written documentation outlining the scope of the role, its impact, the responsibilities and other essential requirements. This often involves drawing on comparable placements we’ve made and being candid about what’s realistic in the current talent market. Search and Identification Our search draws on a combination of our extensive global network, direct outreach and referrals from trusted contacts across the global family office community. Many of the candidates we approach aren’t visible on the open market and access to them comes from our highly established and trusted relationships. Assessment and Screening A thorough evaluation of potential candidates, including in- depth personal interviews, verification of experience and credentials and determination of cultural compatibility is completed. This provides the client with an adequate basis for independent and expert recommendations. A behavioural assessment tool is often employed as part of the assessment. Presentation and Interview Support Only the most qualified candidates are presented to clients. We submit concise oral and written reports that include information about employment and salary history, education, management abilities, product, market, and technical knowledge, reporting relationships, communication skills, and those personal intangibles that create the cultural fit. Interviews Interviews with candidates that clients wish to meet are scheduled at the earliest possible opportunity. As family office recruiters, we facilitate and prepare both sides for the interview process, and we’re actively involved throughout. Reference and Background Checks Information obtained in the reference checking process is critical to the family office recruitment process. Our detailed and time-tested methodology provides clients with the appropriate insights from people who know the candidate best, former managers, peers and subordinates. We also conduct background checks including DBS, fiscal and social media screening. Negotiation Candidates are often more likely to share their incentives with a third party. This places us in a unique position to assist our clients in structuring a competitive compensation package that fits into family office parameters whilst providing appropriate incentive to the candidate. Offer and Placement We manage the offer process carefully, acting as an honest broker when needed. Once an appointment is made, our family office recruitment firm remains in contact with both the client and the placed candidate to ensure a smooth transition, accelerating working relations and positive impact of the new hire. Types of Family Office Positions We Work on - From Executive, Finance to Legal We place across a variety of family office positions, from entry-level through to C-suite. The family office jobs we’re most regularly engaged for include: Executive and Leadership Chief Executive Officers , Chiefs of Staff , Heads of Family Office and senior advisors operating at the strategic heart of the office. Investment Chief Investment Officers , Portfolio Managers, Investment Directors, Private Equity Associates, Real Assets leads, and Analysts across public markets, private equity, real estate and alternatives. Finance Chief Financial Officers , Finance Directors, Controllers, Heads of Tax and Tax Advisors, and finance executives experienced in complex, multi-jurisdictional structures. Legal and Compliance General Counsel, Heads of Legal, Compliance Officers, and governance professionals who understand the regulatory landscape of private wealth structures. Operations and Administration Chief Operating Officers , Operations Managers, Executive Assistants, Personal Assistants, Office Managers, and wider business support staff who form the operational backbone of a well-run office. For household and estate staffing needs, we work alongside our sister company Cora , ensuring clients can access a full recruitment service, suited to the full breadth of their lifestyle, across both corporate and private functions, around the world. Why Clients Choose Eagle Private We focus our search practice on providing a bespoke service within the industry and deliver exceptional results for our clients. A reputation worth responding to The most sought-after candidates are rarely looking. They are often already employed, well compensated and settled. Identifying, approaching and securing this calibre of individual requires deep market knowledge, established relationships and a reputation worth responding to. As retained executive search consultants, we consistently deliver the very best professionals with the speed and discretion our clients require. Relationships built on trust Our family office recruitment firm is built on long-term relationships established over many years. A large number of our clients have been with us since the beginning; and frequently candidates we placed years ago come back to us when they’re looking for their next career move. That continuity matters tremendously in a market built on trust. A highly transparent and honest approach We don’t simply present candidates to ensure a shortlist – if the right person isn’t out there, or if the brief needs refining, we will give honest feedback. We are transparent in our approach and pride ourselves on having open, ongoing conversations with our clients throughout the process. We understand the human dimension As a family office recruitment agency, we know that the best plac",
