#### Nela Krásná [...] Zaměřuje se také na rozvíjení vztahů s nejvýznamnějšími klienty kanceláře a strategickými obchodními partnery v ČR, na Slovensku i v zahraničí. Díky svým dlouholetým zkušenostem, renomé, mimořádnému pracovnímu nasazení, včetně jedinečných kontaktů v právnických a podnikatelských kruzích v ČR a na Slovensku, je vyhledáván špičkovými českými i slovenskými podnikateli, investory a manažery.",Homepage - One Family Office,,,2026-07-28T09:54:52.828058,Corporate Development and M&A Teams,,Validation score: 6,Verified,,,EXISTING,,,,,Tavily,,"['filip.cabart@onefamilyoffice.cz', 'ondrej.florian@onefamilyoffice.cz', 'jaroslav.havel@onefamilyoffice.cz', 'info@onefamilyoffice.cz', 'michal.klucar@onefamilyoffice.sk', 'stepan.starha@onefamilyoffice.sk', 'jasna.zejnilovic@onefamilyoffice.cz']","Homepage - One Family Office Skip to content Menu Connected through success ONE FAMILY OFFICE, a unique business and investor club, together with its team of nearly twenty experienced investment professionals and a cooperating private-client team of the law firm HAVEL & PARTNERS comprising approximately 50 legal, tax, and accounting advisors, represents the largest family office in Central Europe in terms of capacity. The activities of ONE FAMILY OFFICE are built on three fundamental pillars : (1) investment and management of family assets ; (2) advisory and protection of family wealth , and (3) concierge services – ensuring the highest possible quality of life for the family . The concierge services cover four primary areas of interest for high-net-worth families and are provided at a level unavailable to any individuals other than the members and affiliated members of ONE FAMILY OFFICE in the Czech Republic and Slovakia. These areas include: Prevention and maintenance of health; Comprehensive family security, including cybersecurity and reputation protection; Support and development of the next generation; Philanthropy in the broadest sense. ONE FAMILY OFFICE has a direct presence not only in the Czech Republic and Slovakia, but also in Frankfurt, Dubai, and London. It focuses on a high-yield, balanced, and maximally secure globally diversified asset portfolio across all major world currencies, including the possibility of arranging a regular annuity for partner families that no longer generate significant income from active business operations. The combined assets of founders, partners, and a limited circle of business associates participating in the ONE FAMILY OFFICE platform amount to CZK 18 billion . We provide comprehensive advisory services related to the establishment, structuring, and ongoing management of family, foundation, and trust funds both domestically and abroad. We have created more than 550 family foundation funds, trust funds, and foreign trusts, with the total value of assets under management through our structures exceeding CZK 230 billion . The associated members, members and co-investors of ONE FAMILY OFFICE are typically high-net-worth families and individuals with total available assets of at least CZK 100 million (for full-scope services). However, for co-investment opportunities, we also work with partners with significantly lower asset volumes, including successful executives with strong and regular annual cash flow. ONE FAMILY OFFICE continues to welcome additional high-net-worth families and individuals. If you are interested in cooperation with a multi-family office in wealth protection and management, concierge services, or joint investments, please contact any of our partners. ONE FAMILY OFFICE – Solid Foundation for Further Success The largest and best-staffed multi-family office in the Czech Republic and Slovakia: nearly 20 internationally experienced investment specialists and approximately 50 cooperating legal, tax, and accounting advisors Built on the partners and long-term contacts of Havel & Partners (by far the largest Czech attorneys-at-law and a member of the TOP 100 most valuable Czech companies according to Deloitte) The largest share in handling family succession, creation and management of family wealth structures, i.e., family foundations and holdings, with more than 550 family structures created in the Czech Republic and Slovakia Opportunity to cooperate with the best and long-established global managers of alternative assets – private equity, private credit, venture capital, and hedge funds In 2024, we allocated over USD 100 million in this way, with a plan to exceed USD 200 million in 2025 Absolute overview of domestic investment opportunities, which we are able to identify thanks to a unique ecosystem of cooperating entrepreneurs and co-investors of ONE FAMILY OFFICE, the Advisory Board, and also the strongest attorneys-at-law in the Czech-Slovak region with a team of more than 100 M&A specialists – we regularly supplement our portfolio with the most interesting of these opportunities More info … ONE FAMILY OFFICE – Solid Foundation for Further Success × We are a state-of-the-art multifamily office providing comprehensive advisory services to creditworthy families and individuals. ONE FAMILY OFFICE is a unique and integrated combination of advisory services for the management, protection and preservation of client assets in the Czech Republic, Slovakia and abroad . We provide our partners with an exceptionally extensive information range on local or foreign investments/co-investments . We provide expert service in designing an appropriate private wealth structure taking into account the needs and specifics of the family or individual. Our aim is to present and ensure the implementation of a solution to our business partners that maximizes the protection of the accumulated wealth from external influences and family or personal tragedies or storms, while allowing for the prudent management and preservation of assets. It goes without saying that a tax optimisation is also part of our services. The ONE FAMILY OFFICE relies on top-notch advisory services necessary for the efficient and smart stewardship, protection and preservation of our partners’ assets to the fullest extent. This includes in particular law, tax, accounting, corporate finance, etc. Of course, this service covers comprehensive fiduciary and trust services – everything regarding foundation, trust, investment or other ownership structures in the Czech Republic, Slovakia and worldwide. Close Services Succession Planning for Family Businesses ↓ Endowment Funds and Trusts, Foreign Trusts ↓ Investment Opportunities with Global Reach ↓ Care for Family Health and Safety, Development of the Next Generation ↓ Philanthropy ↓ Asset Management ↓ Family and Succession Planning ↓ Arbitration and mediation ↓ Tax, Accounting and Corporate Governance ↓ Fiduciary service ↓ International Reach Investing in a Global Environment ↓ Foreign Investments Zahraniční investice ↓ Global Advisory ↓ Our Approach We pride ourselves on strong value pillars such as strategic thinking, individual approach, a top-notch team and building long-term partnerships. When founding the ONE FAMILY OFFICE, we were mainly inspired by the principles of Warren Buffett and Charlie Munger of Berkshire Hathaway, who are considered the best investors since World War II. The concept is also based on the principles and personality of David Swensen , founder and pioneer of the Endowment investment model. Under his leadership spanning nearly 40 years, the Yale University endowment achieved quite extraordinary results. Indeed, we believe that success is not just about short-term gains, but also about vision, patience, and an emphasis on values and ethics. Strategic Thinking monitoring international trends consolidating your position as an (intellectual) leader and further development strategic thinking and effective management monitoring international trends the latest know-how and technology consolidating your position as an (intellectual) leader and further development Long-term Partnership individual approach and exceptional level of support comprehensive, high value-added services mutually beneficial strategic partnerships individual approach and exceptional level of support comprehensive, high value-added services mutual respect, trust and loyalty Leading Experts people as the most valuable asset stable, loyal and efficient team dedicated top experts with international experience people as the most valuable asset stable, loyal and efficient team support for career growth and diversity Corporate Social Responsibility and Sustainability sustainability, reliability and ethics excellent reputation and economic stability market leader’s responsibility towards society as a whole sustainability, reliability and ethics excellent reputation and economic stability professional risk management T",
c5ab27fe-8904-476c-8ce3-c5ac6af4172e,Corp Dev and M&A Teams,https://archive.familyoffice.com/learning-programs/webinars/private-call-may-17-2016,VERIFIED_FAMILY_OFFICE,0.95,Verified via explicit name cross-matching and signature patterns.,6,,,"Brett Newman is a Managing Director in the Corporate Development Group. Since joining Blackstone in 2007, Mr. Newman has worked on various strategic initiatives on behalf of the firm, including acquisitions, joint ventures, partnerships and divestitures. As a member of Blackstone’s M&A advisory business until 2014, Mr. Newman also worked with a wide range of third-party clients on numerous transactions in the asset management, specialty finance and health insurance industries. Prior to joining Blackstone, Mr. Newman spent six years at PricewaterhouseCoopers, where he provided M&A diligence, valuation and structuring services as a member of the transaction advisory practice. Mr. Newman received a BS in finance and accounting from Bowling Green State University and an MBA with high honors","Private Call - May 17, 2016 | Family Office Exchange",,,2026-07-28T09:54:52.828058,Corp Dev and M&A Teams,,Validation score: 4,Needs Review,,,EXISTING,,,,"As the low rate environment persists, those who are reviewing their alternative investment strategy might do well to consider making reinsurance part of their allocation. Investors should look closely at the new reinsurance model in particular, which is expected to be a growth engine in the reinsurance industry as it provides investors with attractive returns through a tax efficient structure. FOX members have asked for information on innovative investment opportunities.",Tavily,,[],"Private Call - May 17, 2016 | Family Office Exchange Skip to main content Search Search Close Private Call - May 17, 2016 Overview Tuesday, May 17, 2016 - 01:00pm to 02:00pm CDT As the low rate environment persists, those who are reviewing their alternative investment strategy might do well to consider making reinsurance part of their allocation. Investors should look closely at the new reinsurance model in particular, which is expected to be a growth engine in the reinsurance industry as it provides investors with attractive returns through a tax efficient structure. FOX members have asked for information on innovative investment opportunities. In response, and because the reinsurance trend is significant, FOX is pleased to invite a select group of family office members to participate in this unique private call for the opportunity to learn about reinsurance and closely examine a reinsurance product in the context of education. This opportunity is made possible through our relationship with CAIS, a FOX Thought Leader Council member. Stephen A. Schwarzman, chairman, CEO and co-founder of Blackstone will start the investment conversation by commenting on important trends and opportunities impacting family offices and the need for the alignment of interests between asset managers and investors. Ben Rubin, executive vice president, AXIS Reinsurance, and Brett Newman, managing director in Blackstone’s Corporate Development Group, will provide the following: Introductory overview of reinsurance risk and reinsurance companies Explanation of reinsurance as a new operating model for generating returns Description of the potential market opportunity for publicly traded reinsurance companies Exploration of the benefits of investing in alternative strategies through a reinsurance company Presentation of Harrington Re, which AXIS Capital Holdings and Blackstone have partnered to sponsor and launch All attendees are encouraged to take advantage of this opportunity to tap into our speakers’ expertise by bringing their questions to the call. FOX investment network members will also be invited to continue the discussion privately within their network communities via their online discussion groups. Note: FOX is offering this call for educational purposes only and does not endorse this or any type of specific investment or this specific product. Recommended for: FOX Investment Network Members Sign in to register Sign In FOX Members & Public Network Guests: Email Address * Password * Create Guest Account Request new password SIGN IN NEW ACCOUNT Speaker(s) Stephen A. Schwarzman, Chairman, CEO and Co-Founder, Blackstone Stephen A. Schwarzman is Chairman, CEO and Co-Founder of Blackstone. Mr. Schwarzman has been involved in all phases of the firm’s development since its founding in 1985. The firm is a leading global asset manager with $344 billion Assets Under Management (as of March 31, 2016). Mr. Schwarzman is an active philanthropist with a history of supporting education and schools. Whether in business or in philanthropy, he has always attempted to tackle big problems and find transformative solutions. In 2015, Mr. Schwarzman donated $150 million to Yale University to establish the Schwarzman Center, a first-of-its-kind campus center in Yale’s historic “Commons” building. In 2013, he founded an international scholarship program, “Schwarzman Scholars,” at Tsinghua University in Beijing to educate future leaders about China. At $450 million, the program is modeled on the Rhodes Scholarship and is the single largest philanthropic effort in China’s history coming largely from international donors. In 2007, Mr. Schwarzman donated $100 million to the New York Public Library on whose board he serves. Mr. Schwarzman is a member of The Council on Foreign Relations, The Business Council, The Business Roundtable, and The International Business Council of the World Economic Forum. He is co-chair of the Partnership for New York City and serves on the boards of The Asia Society and New York-Presbyterian Hospital, as well as on The Advisory Board of the School of Economics and Management at Tsinghua University, Beijing. He is a Trustee of The Frick Collection in New York City and Chairman Emeritus of the Board of Directors of The John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts. In 2007, Mr. Schwarzman was included in TIME’s “100 Most Influential People.” Mr. Schwarzman was awarded the Légion d'Honneur of France in 2007 and promoted to Officier in 2010. Ben Rubin, Executive Vice President, AXIS Reinsurance Ben Rubin was appointed Executive Vice President at AXIS Reinsurance to lead the company’s third party capital business in 2013. Prior to joining AXIS, Mr. Rubin worked at Merrill Lynch in insurance investment banking where his experience encompassed capital raising, mergers and acquisitions and risk transfer solutions globally. Responsible for originating, structuring and executing financing and capital solutions across the insurance sector, Ben has experience introducing alternative sources of capital into the insurance and reinsurance market. Brett Newman, Managing Director-Corporate Development Group, Blackstone Brett Newman is a Managing Director in the Corporate Development Group. Since joining Blackstone in 2007, Mr. Newman has worked on various strategic initiatives on behalf of the firm, including acquisitions, joint ventures, partnerships and divestitures. As a member of Blackstone’s M&A advisory business until 2014, Mr. Newman also worked with a wide range of third-party clients on numerous transactions in the asset management, specialty finance and health insurance industries. Prior to joining Blackstone, Mr. Newman spent six years at PricewaterhouseCoopers, where he provided M&A diligence, valuation and structuring services as a member of the transaction advisory practice. Mr. Newman received a BS in finance and accounting from Bowling Green State University and an MBA with high honors from the University of Chicago Booth School of Business.",
