03616b0e-b06a-47cf-a195-452e21d0a57b,Leading Multi Family Office in London,https://www.patronuspartners.com/multi-family-office-in-london,VERIFIED_FAMILY_OFFICE,0.95,Verified via explicit name cross-matching and signature patterns.,10,,,"A leading multi family office based in London. Spears Magazine's 'Top 10 Wealth Manager in the UK"" Book a Free 1 Hour Consultation.",Leading Multi Family Office in London | Patronus Partners — Patronus Partners,,,2026-07-28T09:57:49.556253,Leading Multi Family Office in London,,Validation score: 10,Verified,,nfo@patronuspartners.com,EXISTING,,,02038185300,"A leading multi family office based in London. Spears Magazine's 'Top 10 Wealth Manager in the UK"" Book a Free 1 Hour Consultation.",Tavily,,"['7HRinfo@patronuspartners.com02038185300', '4SAinfo@patronuspartners.com02038185300']","Leading Multi Family Office in London | Patronus Partners — Patronus Partners 1000ms 100vh 0 Multi-family office in London Patronus Partners is a multi-family office in London. Spear's Magazine 'Top 10 Wealth Managers in the UK’ (James Barton). A multi-family office in London Patronus was founded in 2015 on the realisation that large wealth management firms are often sub-optimal for clients. Patronus is an increasingly rare example of a genuinely independent, unconflicted, staff owned multi-family office in London offering family-office wealth management. Our clients benefit from our team’s experience working for large banks, hedge funds and investment firms but prefer a more intimate, friendly and client focused multi-family office. We prefer to stay small, independent and optimal for a limited number of discerning families. What we do Financial Advice We structure our client’s investment portfolios as tax efficiently as possible. We monitor changes in government legislation to make sure that our clients remain as tax efficient as possible and give ongoing advice on this. We do not charge initial fees for financial advice. Investment Management A changing investment environment requires adaptation, innovation, and focus. As a multi-family office in London, we are able to offer a flexible investment style, in order to capitalise on the ever changing macroeconomic environment. We can actively position portfolios, whatever the evolving investment landscape, and, as we are an independent multi-family office in London, we are entirely free to invest in an unconflicted way, with no “in-house” products. You can read some of our latest research here. Trading Some of our clients also use our execution only trading and custody service, enabling them to have all of their investments under one roof. Our traders work on behalf of various, hedge funds and family offices. Our private clients are able to benefit from institutional quality trading, settlement and custody. Arrange A Call “We are all escapees from large firms and feel that clients no longer want the bland industry stereotype but prefer a smaller firm whose interests are aligned with theirs. The industry is ever- homogenising and unfortunately seems to focus more on shareholders than on clients"". — James Barton, Spear’s magazine. The Unspoken Truth… is that large pension advice firms are often sub-optimal for their clients. As an independent pension advisor we are not constrained by being tied to our own in-house funds, looking after too many clients and nor are we under relentless shareholder pressure for revenue growth – all of which are detrimental to clients. Our clients receive truly independent advice about their pensions in an unbiased way. We only ever offer what we believe to be the best in class in order to deliver the best outcome for our clients. ""Patronus’ from the original Latin, is a person who stood as a protector to another, who was called his ‘client’. It struck a chord with us.” — Paul Kavanagh CEO Why invest with a multi-family office in London? Independence We are employee owned with no shareholder pressure to deliver ever increasing revenue targets, which are often to the detriment of the client. Freedom We are not constrained or conflicted by the issues many pension advice firms face such as being tied to their own ’in-house’ funds and static portfolios. We are free to invest in what we believe will give the best outcome. Performance Whilst we cannot guarantee that past performance will be repeated, since inception, our portfolios have performed better than the industry benchmark. Experience Most members of our team have over 20 years’ experience looking after the investments for private clients and working in senior positions of larger firms. Close Relationships We deliberately have fewer clients so that they can benefit from an intimate relationship with the firm and have direct access to our whole team in Berkshire and London. Fees We do not charge initial fees for our advice just a clear annual fee, only payable once you start to invest with us. Schedule a Phone Call Paul Kavanagh Director Read Bio Jeremy Steinson Director Read Bio S-J Kavanagh Operations Read Bio James Barton Investment Director Read Bio John Prior Director, CIO Read Bio Kareem Khouri Director, COO Read Bio Dan Dowding Head of Wealth Management Read Bio Penny Rooney Head of Compliance Read Bio Richard Griffiths Trading Manager Read Bio Harriet Harrison Operations Read Bio Jonathan Jackson Head of Research Read Bio James Blackmore Trader Read Bio × Arrange a Free Consultation Arrange A Call Pick a convenient time to speak to one of our team. Choose a Time Book Free Consultation Arrange a time to receive a free consultation. Book Meeting Email Us Get in touch to ask us any questions. Email “One of the top 10 Wealth Managers in the UK. Barton is a dichotomy... An affable bonhomie, but with a sharp, disruptive, forward-thinking mind. His preference for questioning the rules, combined with his friendly nature, is why clients seek his insightful advice and why he is regarded as one of the top practitioners in the industry"" — James Barton’s Review in Spear’s Magazine London 68 King William Street, London. EC4N 7HR i nfo@patronuspartners.com 02038185300 Berkshire 1650 Arlington Business Park, Reading, Berkshire. RG7 4SA i nfo@patronuspartners.com 02038185300 What is a multi-family office in London? Unveiling the Discreet Guardians of Wealth: A Deep Dive into UK Family Offices In the opulent tapestry of London's financial landscape, a select group of entities operate silently yet powerfully, safeguarding the financial well-being of affluent families across generations. These discreet entities, known as family offices, stand as pillars of wealth preservation and strategic growth, offering a unique blend of financial acumen and personalized service. Understanding ""what is a Family Office"" becomes paramount for discerning individuals in the UK seeking to optimize their wealth management strategies and navigate the intricacies of their financial futures. Beyond Bricks and Mortar: Unveiling the Multifaceted Family Office Ecosystem The term ""family office"" encompasses two distinct models: Single Family Offices (SFOs) and Multi-Family Offices (MFOs). Each carries its own set of advantages and considerations. SFOs, as the name suggests, cater exclusively to the needs of a single family, offering an unparalleled level of personalization and bespoke service. This exclusivity, however, often comes at a significant cost, requiring substantial financial resources to establish and maintain a dedicated team of professionals. Multi Family Offices, on the other hand, provide wealth management services to multiple families, leveraging economies of scale to offer efficient and cost-effective solutions. They are particularly prevalent in financial hubs like London, attracting families seeking professional guidance without the hefty price tag associated with an Single Family Offices. Multi Family Offices often boast diverse teams of experts, ensuring access to a wider range of specialized knowledge and experience. Beyond Investment Management: A Symphony of Services Orchestrated by Family Offices While ""family office wealth management"" remains a core function, their services extend far beyond mere investment strategies. A comprehensive family office acts as a central hub, orchestrating a symphony of financial, legal, and lifestyle management services: • Investment Management: Tailored investment strategies are crafted, meticulously aligned with the family's risk tolerance and long-term goals, encompassing traditional and alternative asset classes. • Tax Planning: Complex tax optimization strategies are implemented to minimize liabilities and ensure intergenerational wealth transfer through sophisticated estate planning techniques. • Estate Planning: Wills, trusts, and other legal instruments are meticulously structured to safeguard ass",
