 ####",Gupta Capital Group,,,2026-07-28T09:59:46.953323,Gupta Goyal Revocable Â Trust,,Validation score: 4,Needs Review,,,EXISTING,,,,,Tavily,,[],"Gupta Capital Group 0 Gupta Capital Group We are a single family office with 40 years of experience in nurturing sustainable business growth while actively giving back to the community. Learn more about us Investment Strategy Gupta Capital has a broad portfolio managed through three primary investment verticals: Control Private Equity, Minority Private Investments and Asset Management. learn more Portfolio Companies Gupta Capital Group is the parent company to a dynamic group of portfolio companies focused on steel and metals manufacturing and distribution. Our strategy focuses on utilizing the various capabilities of the family office and its management team to enable long term growth. learn more Philanthropy Founded in 2005, the Gupta Agarwal Foundation is a passion shared by Satish and Yasmin. The Foundation seeks to promote access to education, health care, and cultural awareness. learn more Team — Gupta Capital Group 0 About Us Gupta Capital Group is a single family office engaged in sustainably growing a diversified portfolio of operating businesses and other investments. Over the past 40 years, we’ve developed long-term permanent capital positions across varied investments and portfolio companies. Our Story Leading our family office are Satish and Yasmin Gupta. While Satish and Yasmin were earning their MBAs at the University of Dallas, Satish launched SB International with an idea and a $10,000 investment from one of his professors. After finding quick success, he eventually grew SB International from an international metals trading operation to one of the largest suppliers of Oil Country Tubular Goods in the country. Over the following 40 years Satish and Yasmin started and acquired other businesses in the steel and metals industry and invested across other asset classes to build Gupta Capital Group into the highly diversified family enterprise it is today. Satish and Yasmin continually give of themselves in a variety of philanthropic causes, most notably health care and research, higher education, and cultural awareness activities. — Our Team Michael Fielding General Counsel Michael Fielding is General Counsel of Gupta Capital Group and has oversight of all legal functions and responsibilities for the family office as well as its portfolio companies. In addition to his duties as General Counsel, he is also actively involved in strategic planning, mergers and acquisitions, joint ventures, and other business development activities. Before joining SB International in 2010, Mr. Fielding worked as an Associate in the Corporate Department of Baker Botts L.L.P. in Houston, Texas, where he represented both public and private company clients in mergers and acquisitions, equity and debt offerings, and other business transactions. Mr. Fielding graduated summa cum laude from the University of Utah with a bachelor’s degree in Finance, and he received his Juris Doctor degree, with high honors, from Brigham Young University. Before law school, Mr. Fielding worked for IBM as a Financial Analyst in Chicago, Illinois. Willie Stewart Chief Investment Officer Willie Stewart is the Chief Investment Officer of Gupta Capital Group where he oversees its overall investment strategy and leads its merger and acquisition activities. He also serves as an internal resource to our portfolio companies on strategy and growth initiatives. Prior to joining Gupta Capital in 2018, Willie spent 11 years with the family office of Nelson Bunker Hunt in Dallas where he served in various roles including as an Advisory Board Member. In these roles he focused on direct private investments in the oil and gas sector where he was involved in dozens of completed transactions and helped manage a diverse multi asset class investment portfolio. He holds a BS in Economics with Finance Applications from Southern Methodist University and an MBA with concentration in Finance from Northwestern University’s Kellogg School of Management. Gary McNeil Chief HR Officer Gary McNeil joined Gupta Capital Group as the Chief Human Resource Officer in 2019. Gary is actively involved in a variety of business initiatives aimed at continually improving the business and our talent. Prior to Gupta Capital, he held executive level HR leadership roles with Fortive Corporation, AkzoNobel, and The Sherwin-Williams Company, both domestically and internationally. He has led large, globally-dispersed teams as a division level business partner in the full scope of human capital management, including strategy, talent acquisition and management, organization design and development, mergers and acquisitions, change management, performance improvement, among others. Mr. McNeil graduated from Texas A&M University - Kingsville, with a BBA in Finance, and from Amberton University - Dallas, with an MBA. Following his undergraduate degree, Gary served as a reserve officer in the U.S. Air Force. The Family Satish Gupta President Satish Gupta founded SB International, Inc. in 1981 while pursuing his MBA at the University of Dallas and built SB into one of the largest international products suppliers and processors of pipe and tubing for the oil and gas industry. In addition to growing SB throughout the last 40 years, Satish started and acquired other steel and metals related businesses and began investing across other industries and asset classes to build Gupta Capital into the highly diversified family enterprise it is today. He serves as a Trustee of the Southwestern Medical Foundation and a member of the Board of the Crow Collection of Asian Art in Dallas. Mr. Gupta founded the Gupta Agarwal Charitable Foundation to support education, public health, medical research and the promotion of diversity and cultural awareness. He has been recognized for multiple business and entrepreneurship awards in the Dallas community. Satish graduated with a degree in Economics from Loyola College in Chennai, India and an MBA in International Trade and Management from the University of Dallas. In 2013, Mr. Gupta graduated from the OPM executive education program at Harvard Business School. In April 2013, he was privileged to be among the first honorees at the installation of the University of Dallas, College of Business Chapter of the International Honor Society Beta Gamma Sigma (BGS). Yasmin Gupta Executive Vice President Yasmin Gupta is Director and Executive Vice President of SB International, Inc. She holds a degree in public relations from Stella Maris College in Chennai, India and earned an MBA from the University of Dallas in International Trade and Management. Ms. Gupta is a founding Director of State Bank of Texas, a local bank in the DFW Metroplex, and continues to serve as a member of the Board and on various committees. In 2013, she was awarded the privilege of being among the first honorees inducted into the Beta Gamma Sigma (BGS) International Honor Society at the University of Dallas, College of Business Chapter. In 2014, a generous gift from Yasmin and her husband Satish Gupta made possible the state-of-the-art SB Hall, home to the College of Business at the University of Dallas, Irving, Texas. Today, the College of Business for which they are namesakes, has over 17,000 alumni and currently enrolls nearly 1,000 graduate and undergraduate students. She has been involved with several community organizations including the Girl Scouts, United Way, Chinmaya Mission and the DFW Indian Cultural Society. She is also a contributor to the Primary Care Clinic of North Texas, providing medical care to uninsured adults in their three non-profit healthcare facilities since 2003, and the GDAS Cancer Clinic providing non-profit cancer treatment and care to uninsured patients in the metroplex. Kiran Gupta Principal Kiran Gupta is a Principal at Gupta Capital Group. She was previously an HR Business Partner and Executive Coach at Google, where she helped leaders navigate complexity and increase productivity through emotional intelligence. She ea",
